    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate looking to consolidate offensive gains, led by **Yordan Alvarez** (78.66), who stands as our premier start. Facing a mid-tier arm in Perkins, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a massive park factor boost and an elite xwOBA profile that makes him the cornerstone of our lineup. Following closely is **Junior Caminero** (68.59), whose role in the cleanup spot against Nola provides a high-floor opportunity to drive in runs. We are also capitalizing on favorable matchup data for **Lars Nootbaar** (65.85) and **Josh Smith** (64.66); specifically, **Josh Smith** earns a significant boost from facing a pitcher with a slow delivery, which optimizes his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical commodity in our current 5x5 standing.\n\nRegarding the bench, **Dillon Dingler** (36.38) remained our most difficult omission. While he possesses some utility against slower pitchers, his overall efficiency score failed to clear our 40-point floor, primarily due to a tough matchup against Yates and a negative platoon split that neutralized his minor speed advantages. We are also exercising caution with **Carson Benge** (45.62), who remains in the lineup but is on high alert; his score is dragged down significantly by a poor platoon alignment against Early. If we see any mid-game defensive shifts or late-inning pinch-hitting moves, we are prepared to leverage **Casey Schmitt** or **Pedro Ramirez** to maintain our efficiency mandates. As the season winds down, we are proceeding with **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto** in middle-of-the-order roles, hoping their recent contact consistency holds against the Lowder and Mathews matchups, despite the inherent volatility of their respective splits.",
